1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,920
这是 Daily Frontier Papers。
This is Daily Frontier Papers.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,960
今天的论文由 ByteDance 主导，名为 Axion 1.0。
Today's paper is led by ByteDance, and it's called Axion One.

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,644
副标题是「核心观点」。
The subtitle is The Pitch.

4
00:00:09,102 --> 00:00:10,948
开放的智能体基础模型。
Open Agent Foundation Models.

5
00:00:11,438 --> 00:00:11,920
简化版。
Simplified.

6
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:13,440
它背后的问题很直接。
The question behind it is blunt.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,720
今天训练一个强大的智能体模型时，你到底需要多少复杂的训练流程？
When you train a strong agent model today, how much of that long training pipeline do you actually need?

8
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:19,760
先说点背景。
Some context.

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,080
语言模型正在变成智能体。
Language models are turning into agents.

10
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:27,280
它们会搜索、运行代码、调用工具，并处理需要多个步骤的任务。
They search, run code, call tools, and work through tasks that take many steps.

11
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:29,636
构建它们的流程一直在变长。
The pipelines that build them keep growing.

12
00:00:30,062 --> 00:00:35,280
中间训练、好几个监督微调阶段、偏好优化、强化学习。
Mid-training, several supervised stages, preference optimization, reinforcement learning.

13
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:43,440
作者的观点是，虽然每个环节都有其合理性，但堆叠在一起
时，很难判断哪些是关键的，而且整个过程的复现成本很高。
The author's point is that each piece may be well motivated, but stacked together, it's hard to tell which ones matter,
and the whole thing is expensive to reproduce.

14
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,720
还有第二个问题。
There's a second problem.

15
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,880
许多所谓的开放模型只发布权重，几乎没提供别的。
Many so-called open models release their weights and little else.

16
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:52,080
数据是如何构建、过滤和验证的，依然是保密的。
How the data was built, filtered, and verified stays private.

17
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:53,840
论文列举了几个近期的系统。
The paper names a few recent systems.

18
00:00:54,158 --> 00:01:00,880
MuralThinker 1.7 结合了中间训练、监督微调、偏好优化和强化学习。
MuralThinker 1.7 combines mid-training, supervised fine-tuning, preference optimization, and RL.

19
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:01,572
智能体。
Agents.

20
00:01:02,222 --> 00:01:05,360
A1 使用了基于策略的领域路由蒸馏。
A1 uses domain-routed on policy distillation.

21
00:01:05,582 --> 00:01:10,560
Apidex 1.1 探索了可执行环境和多个智能体的协同。
Apidex 1.1 explores executable environments and coordinating multiple agents.

22
00:01:10,734 --> 00:01:14,000
在数据方面，Evo Instruct 让任务变得更难。
On the data side, Evo Instruct makes tasks harder.

23
00:01:14,286 --> 00:01:22,080
通过反复重写，TaskCraft 扩展了可验证的多工具任
务，而 WebShaper 为复杂的搜索任务提供了结构。
Through repeated rewriting, TaskCraft expands verifiable multi-tool
tasks, and WebShaper gives structure to the complexity of search tasks.

24
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:27,280
Axion 的核心思想是：简化流程，但不要简化学习问题。
Axion's key idea: simplify the pipeline, but don't simplify the learning problem.

25
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:30,720
把精力花在困难且可自动验证的数据上。
Put the effort into data that is hard and automatically verifiable.

26
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:32,548
训练只有三个步骤。
Training has just three steps.

27
00:01:33,166 --> 00:01:37,040
两个轻量级的监督微调阶段，然后是强化学习。
Two light supervised fine-tuning stages, then reinforcement learning.

28
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:42,000
没有专门的中间训练，没有 DPO，也没有在策略上的蒸馏。
No dedicated mid-training, no DPO, no on-policy distillation.

29
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:45,348
第一阶段教授不需要外部信息的推理。
Stage one teaches reasoning that needs no outside information.

30
00:01:45,998 --> 00:01:51,120
第二阶段教授带工具的推理，而强化学习则强化长程、多步骤的交互。
Stage two teaches reasoning with tools, and RL hardens long, multi-step interaction.

31
00:01:51,370 --> 00:01:53,120
这里的“开放”不仅仅是指权重。
And open here means more than weights.

32
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:59,920
数据构建、过滤、验证、提示词以及训练代码全部公开。
Data construction, filtering, verification, prompts, and training code are all released.

33
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:04,260
首先是第一阶段的数据，论文称之为“自包含推理”。
Start with the stage one data, which the paper calls self-contained reasoning.

34
00:02:04,782 --> 00:02:06,160
所有需要的信息都在问题里。
Everything you need is in the question.

35
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:12,292
作者收集了数学、物理、化学、生物和计算机科学领域的公开问题。
The authors collect public problems in math, physics, chemistry, biology, and computer science.

36
00:02:12,622 --> 00:02:14,000
但他们并没有直接用这些问题来训练。
But they don't train on them directly.

37
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:16,320
他们把这些问题当作生成更难问题的种子。
They use them as seeds for harder questions.

38
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:17,920
第一步是“组合”。
The first move is composition.

39
00:02:18,094 --> 00:02:24,320
生成模型获取种子解中的某个数值，并编写一个新的问题，要求该数值作为中间结果。
A generator model takes a quantity computed in the seed solution and writes a new question that needs it as an intermediate result.

40
00:02:24,494 --> 00:02:27,600
答案必须是可验证的，且种子信息不能泄露。
The answer must be checkable, and the seed must not leak.

41
00:02:27,694 --> 00:02:28,880
接下来是巧妙的部分。
The clever part comes next.

42
00:02:29,134 --> 00:02:32,560
基础模型尝试用 Python 解决新问题，但不能使用搜索。
The base model tries the new question with Python but no search.

43
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:35,120
如果失败了，该问题就直接进入数据库。
If it fails, the question goes straight into the bank.

44
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:44,800
如果成功了，它的解法会回到生成模型，生成模型会随
机应用四种强化操作，专门针对模型刚刚使用的策略。
If it succeeds, its solution goes back to the generator, which applies one of four hardening operations at random,
aimed squarely at the strategy the model just used.

45
00:02:44,974 --> 00:02:46,480
图中有一个简单的例子。
The figure has a toy example.

46
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:50,000
基础模型知道 1 加到 10 的和是 55。
The base model knows 1 plus 2 up to 10 is 55.

47
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,760
“组合”操作增加了一个步骤。
Composition adds one more step.

48
00:02:51,982 --> 00:02:55,200
“参数化”将 10 替换为 n，并要求给出公式。
Parameterization swaps 10 for n and asks for a formula.

49
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:58,080
“范围偏移”选择一个太大到无法逐项相加的数字。
Range shift picks a number too big to add term by term.

50
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:02,960
“情况分析”交替正负号，因此答案取决于 n 是奇数还是偶数。
Case analysis alternates the signs, so the answer depends on whether n is even or odd.

51
00:03:03,054 --> 00:03:04,400
他们怎么知道答案是正确的？
How do they know the answers are right?

52
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:15,840
GPT 5.5 独立求解每个问题三次，只有当三次结果一致且推导过程正确时，参考答案才被接受。
GPT 5.5 solves each question three times, independently, and the reference
answer is accepted only if all three agree and the derivations check out.

53
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,440
然后，另一个模型来求解数据库，只有正确且格式规范的轨迹才会被保留。
Then a separate model solves the bank, and only correct, well formed trajectories are kept.

54
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,640
图中显示这一阶段产生了 108,000 条轨迹。
The figure puts this stage at 10.8,000 trajectories.

55
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:27,520
第二阶段是关于需要工具的问题。
Stage 2 is about questions that need tools.

56
00:03:27,694 --> 00:03:39,040
作者收集了生物、化学、数学、地理和航空等领域的公开结构化数据，
并使用确定性程序来构建每个问题并计算答案。
The authors gather public structured data in areas like biology, chemistry, math, geography, and aviation,
and use deterministic programs to build each question and compute its answer.

57
00:03:39,662 --> 00:03:44,656
经过过滤、筛选、计算，最后由语言模型将其转化为自然的表达方式。
Filter, select, compute, and finally have a language model phrase it naturally.

58
00:03:44,816 --> 00:03:45,636
这是他们的例子。
Their example.

59
00:03:46,094 --> 00:03:53,572
筛选有环的行星，选择质量最小的一颗，即天王星，并询问其平均密度。
Filter for planets with rings, select the least massive one, which is Uranus, and ask for its mean density.

60
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:57,216
大约是每立方厘米 1.27 克。
About 1.27 grams per cubic centimeter.

61
00:03:57,326 --> 00:04:06,852
求解器必须识别出天王星，查出它的质量和半径，然后进行计算。为了强制模型使用工具，
在求解过程中会屏蔽构造数据库。
The solver has to identify Uranus, look up its mass and radius, and do the math. To force real tool use,
the construction databases are blocked during solving.

62
00:04:07,246 --> 00:04:14,096
模型只能使用搜索、网页访问和 Python，而那些不需要工具就能回答的问题会被移除。
The model only gets search, web page visits, and Python, and questions answerable without tools are removed.

63
00:04:14,190 --> 00:04:16,579
同样，只有正确的轨迹才能保留下来。
Again, only correct trajectories survive.

64
00:04:17,005 --> 00:04:18,576
一共 7,500 条。
7,500 of them.

65
00:04:18,766 --> 00:04:21,216
第二阶段微调从第一阶段继续进行。
The second fine-tuning stage continues from the first.

66
00:04:21,375 --> 00:04:24,516
损失函数仅针对模型自己生成的内容进行计算。
Loss is computed only on what the model writes itself.

67
00:04:25,006 --> 00:04:27,696
包括它的推理过程、工具调用和最终答案。
Its reasoning, tool calls, and final answer.

68
00:04:27,886 --> 00:04:29,776
工具的输出仅作为上下文。
Tool outputs are context only.

69
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:36,896
第三步是使用 GRPO 进行强化学习，它为每个问题采样多个轨迹，
并将每个轨迹与同组的其他轨迹进行比较。
Step 3 is reinforcement learning with GRPO, which samples several
trajectories per question and compares each with the rest of its group.

70
00:04:37,056 --> 00:04:39,936
奖励机制是，正确的答案可以获得 1 分。
The reward, a correct answer, earns one.

71
00:04:40,096 --> 00:04:43,844
错误的答案如果包含经过验证的中间步骤，仍可获得部分分数。
A wrong answer can still earn partial credit for verified intermediate steps.

72
00:04:44,110 --> 00:04:49,696
最高可得 0.3 分，如果没有提交答案则扣除 0.1 分，且分数永远不会低于 0。
Up to 0.3, minus 0.1 if no answer was submitted, and never below 0.

73
00:04:49,856 --> 00:04:51,616
中间步骤是怎么检查的？
How are intermediate steps checked?

74
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:56,816
第二阶段的程序已经记录了每一个中间结果，比如选择了哪颗行星。
The stage 2 program already recorded every intermediate result, such as which planet was selected.

75
00:04:56,910 --> 00:04:58,564
这些步骤是按照依赖顺序进行检查的。
These are checked in dependency order.

76
00:04:58,990 --> 00:05:01,936
而且只有在之前的所有步骤都正确的情况下，后续步骤才会被计入。
And a later step only counts if every step before it was right.

77
00:05:02,158 --> 00:05:03,456
任务选择也很重要。
Task selection matters too.

78
00:05:03,616 --> 00:05:11,616
当前模型会对每个问题尝试四次，只有当至少有一个尝试
正确，且四个奖励分数不完全一致时，该问题才会被保留。
The current model attempts each question four times, and a question is kept only
if at least one attempt is correct and the four rewards aren't all the same.

79
00:05:11,776 --> 00:05:12,976
还有一个工程细节。
One engineering detail.

80
00:05:13,136 --> 00:05:21,376
Axion 是一个混合专家模型，也就是 MOE，推理引擎
和训练引擎可以将相同的 token 分配给不同的专家。
Axion is a mixture of experts model, or MOE, and the inference engine
and the training engine can route the same token to different experts.

81
00:05:21,536 --> 00:05:26,416
一种叫做 R3 的方法会记录在 rollout 过程中选定的专家，并在训练中重新播放它们。
A method called R3 records the experts chosen during rollout and replays them in training.

82
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:27,136
实验设置。
The setup.

83
00:05:27,296 --> 00:05:29,536
两个主要模型都是混合专家模型。
Both main models are mixture of experts.

84
00:05:29,806 --> 00:05:36,496
一个从 Quen 3.6 初始化出的 35B 模型，以及一个从 Quen 3.5 初始化出的 122B 模型。
A 35B model initialized from Quen 3.6 and a 122B model from Quen 3.5.

85
00:05:36,718 --> 00:05:42,736
在评估时，它们可以使用网页搜索、网页访问、学术检索和 Python。
At evaluation time, they get web search, web page visits, scholarly retrieval, and Python.

86
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:44,096
监督微调的成本很低。
Supervised training is cheap.

87
00:05:44,256 --> 00:05:56,576
122B 模型在 32 块 GPU 上完成两个阶段共耗时 7.5 小
时，大约是 240 GPU 小时；35B 模型大约是 90 小时。
The 122B model takes 7.5 hours for both stages on 32 GPUs, about 240 GPU hours, and the 35B model about 90.

88
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,816
论文中没有给出强化学习的总计算量。
The paper doesn't give total compute for RL.

89
00:05:58,896 --> 00:06:00,816
主要结果在表 1 中。
The main results are in Table 1.

90
00:06:01,006 --> 00:06:04,176
从 Humanity's Last Exam，也就是 HLE 开始。
Start with Humanity's Last Exam, or HLE.

91
00:06:04,462 --> 00:06:06,976
涵盖多个领域的专家级问题。
Expert level questions across many fields.

92
00:06:07,214 --> 00:06:15,136
在屏蔽 Hugging Face 等网站的情况下，35B 模型的得分是 52.2，122B 模型是 59。
With sites like Hugging Face blocked, the 35B model scores 52.2 and the 122B 59.

93
00:06:15,296 --> 00:06:19,456
如果没有这个限制，得分分别是 59.1 和 64.8。
Without that restriction, is 59.1 and 64.8.

94
00:06:19,536 --> 00:06:29,440
与同等规模的开源模型 A1 相比，35B 模型在 HLE 上领先 4.6 分，
在 Search Heavy SEAL 上领先 5.8 分，在 seal 0 上持平，
Against agents A1, an open model of similar size, the 35B model is ahead by 4.6 points
on HLE, 5.8 on the Search Heavy SEAL, 0, and 7 on the Frontier Science Olympiad set.

95
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:33,696
在 Frontier Science Olympiad 数据集上领先 7 分。
Against agents A1, an open model of similar size, the 35B model is ahead by 4.6 points
on HLE, 5.8 on the Search Heavy SEAL, 0, and 7 on the Frontier Science Olympiad set.

96
00:06:33,856 --> 00:06:46,576
在 Frontier Science Research 上，作者测得 122B 模型得分为 66.7，
而 GPT 5.6 soul 为 63.3，A1 为 40，但它并非在所有方面都领先。
On Frontier Science Research, the 122B model scores 66.7 against 63.3 for GPT 5.6 soul as measured by the authors,
and 40 for agents A1, but it doesn't lead everywhere.

97
00:06:46,766 --> 00:06:56,496
在 HLE 上，Claude Fable 5 和 Claude Opus 5 分别
报告为 63.8 和 63.6，高于 Axion 受限状态下的 59。
On HLE, Claude Fable 5 and Claude Opus 5 report 63.8 and 63.6 above Axion's restricted 59.

98
00:06:56,622 --> 00:07:09,856
在 Biomystery Bench 的高难度子集上，122B 模型得分为 41.7，落后于 Claude Opus 5、
GPT 5.6 Soul 和 Claude Fable 5，表 2 展示了每一步带来的提升。
On the hard subset of Biomystery Bench, the 122B models 41.7 trails, Claude
Opus 5, GPT 5.6 Soul, and Claude Fable 5, Table 2 shows what each step adds.

99
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:13,296
这些是训练序列中的检查点，而不是消融实验。
These are checkpoints along the training sequence, not ablations.

100
00:07:13,536 --> 00:07:27,056
对于 35B 模型，在包含 130 个问题的 HLE 子集上，基础分数为 47.7，第一阶段后变为 59.2，
第二阶段后变为 66.2，强化学习后达到 70。
For the 35B model, on a 130 question HLE subset, the base score is 47.7, then 59.2 after stage 1, 66.2 after stage 2, and 70 after RL.

101
00:07:27,246 --> 00:07:30,656
在任务需要查阅和数据分析的地方，工具数据帮助最大。
The tool data helps most where the task needs lookup and data analysis.

102
00:07:31,246 --> 00:07:37,376
35B 模型在 Biomystery Bench 上的得分从 17.6 提高到 35.3。
The 35B model's biomystery bench score goes from 17.6 to 35.3.

103
00:07:37,616 --> 00:07:44,496
奇怪的是，第一阶段反而把同样的得分从 23.5 降到了 17.6。
Oddly, stage 1 had pushed that same score down from 23.5 to 17.6.

104
00:07:44,736 --> 00:07:49,892
强化学习提升了两个尺寸模型在 HLE 子集和 seal 0 上的表现。
RL improves the HLE subset and seal 0 at both sizes.

105
00:07:50,350 --> 00:07:55,776
35B 模型的 seal 0 得分从 53.2 提高到 62.2。
The 35B model's seal 0 goes from 53.2 to 62.2.

106
00:07:55,936 --> 00:07:59,456
但在某些科学推理数据集上，35B 模型略有下滑。
But on some science reasoning sets, the 35B model slips a little.

107
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:06,096
作者总结道：大部分提升来自两个微调阶段，而强化学习在选定的基准测试中增加了更多提升。
The author's summary Much of the gain comes from the two fine-tuning stages, and RL adds more on selected benchmarks.

108
00:08:06,256 --> 00:08:07,296
另外两个实验。
Two more experiments.

109
00:08:07,534 --> 00:08:20,820
从较弱的基座 Quen 3.5（35B）开始，同样的微调将它在 HLE 子集上与 Quen 3.6 的差距从 9.2
分缩小到 0.8 分；而一个仅经过微调、未经过强
Starting from a weaker base, Quen 3.5 at 35B, the same fine-tuning shrinks its HLE subset gap to Quen 3.6 from 9.2 points to 0.8,
and a 9B model with fine-tuning only, no RL, reaches 63.1 on the HLE subset.

110
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:25,216
化学习的 9B 模型在 HLE 子集上达到了 63.1 分。
Starting from a weaker base, Quen 3.5 at 35B, the same fine-tuning shrinks its HLE subset gap to Quen 3.6 from 9.2 points to 0.8,
and a 9B model with fine-tuning only, no RL, reaches 63.1 on the HLE subset.

111
00:08:25,376 --> 00:08:31,616
与 MuralThinker 或 A1 相比，第一个区别是更短的流水线。
Compared with MuralThinker or Agents A1, the first difference is a shorter pipeline.

112
00:08:31,776 --> 00:08:36,868
在数据方面，像 Absolute Zero 和 Agent Zero 这样的工作也会根据模型调整难度。
On data, work like Absolute Zero and Agent Zero also adapts difficulty to the model.

113
00:08:37,326 --> 00:08:42,816
但 Axion 特别强化了基础模型在自身策略下已经能解决的问题。
But Axion specifically hardens the questions the base model already solves along its own strategy.

114
00:08:42,990 --> 00:08:48,096
对于工具任务，程序在语言模型生成问题之前先计算出答案。
For tool tasks, a program computes the answer before a language model writes the question.

115
00:08:48,256 --> 00:08:57,696
尽管如此，论文本身提醒说，表 1 中的许多基准数据来
自官方报告或其他论文，可能使用了不同的工具和设置。
Still, the paper itself cautions that many baseline numbers in table 1 come from
official reports or other papers, with possibly different tools and settings.

116
00:08:57,934 --> 00:09:00,816
这些交叉对比具有参考意义，但并非受控实验。
Those crosshorts comparisons are indicative, not controlled.

117
00:09:00,976 --> 00:09:04,816
我的看法是，这里最有价值的不是任何单一的分数。
My read is that the most valuable thing here isn't any single score.

118
00:09:04,896 --> 00:09:06,336
而是一个可复现的基准。
It's a reproducible baseline.

119
00:09:06,446 --> 00:09:13,776
一个包含数据流水线和代码的三步配方，意味着其他
人可以一次更改一个部分，看看究竟什么才是关键。
A three-step recipe with its data pipelines and code means others can change one piece at a time and see what actually matters.

120
00:09:13,936 --> 00:09:19,216
论文没有单独的局限性章节，但正文中包含几个值得注意的注意事项。
The paper has no separate limitations section, but the text carries several caveats worth noting.

121
00:09:19,376 --> 00:09:21,056
首先是评估协议。
First, the evaluation protocol.

122
00:09:21,454 --> 00:09:31,936
Axion 以及作者自行运行的模型每个基准测试运行三次，Biomystery Bench 运行五次，
论文报告的是单次运行的最佳成绩，而非平均值。
Axion and the models the authors ran themselves get three runs per benchmark, five for Biomystery Bench,
and the paper reports the best single run, not the average.

123
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:40,576
第二，表二是一系列检查点，作者明确表示这不是消融实验，
所以它没法告诉你去掉某一步会发生什么。
Second, table two is a sequence of checkpoints, and the authors say explicitly it's not an ablation,
so it can't tell you what happens if a step is removed.

124
00:09:40,846 --> 00:09:45,376
强化学习的效果也会随模型大小和基准测试而变化，有些分数甚至下降了。
RL's effect also varies by size and benchmark, and some scores went down.

125
00:09:45,536 --> 00:09:50,816
第三，作者表示得分与 R3 的差异不能完全归因于 R3 这一项。
Third, the authors say the score differences with R3 can't be pinned on R3 alone.

126
00:09:50,896 --> 00:09:58,736
而且在加入 R3 后，122B 模型的 Zero 分数从 63.1 降到了 58.6。
And with R3, the 122B models seal, zero fell from 63.1 to 58.6.

127
00:09:58,896 --> 00:10:01,376
第四，模型规模的对比并没有做变量控制。
Fourth, the size comparison isn't controlled.

128
00:10:01,582 --> 00:10:10,576
35B 和 122B 模型从不同的基础模型开始，并且都
经过了强化学习，作者说不应将其视为缩放实验。
The 35B and 122B models start from different bases and also go through
RL, and the authors say it shouldn't be read as a scaling experiment.

129
00:10:10,736 --> 00:10:12,416
论文里关于后续步骤的描述很少。
The paper says little about next steps.

130
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:18,736
它所表达的期望是，发布的训练数据流水线和训练代码能成为未来智能体模型研究的可重复起点。
Its stated hope is that the release data pipelines and training code
become a reproducible starting point for future agent model research.

131
00:10:18,926 --> 00:10:21,412
我的理解是，值得记住的结果是这个。
My read is that the result worth remembering is this.

132
00:10:21,934 --> 00:10:27,296
大部分成效来自于两个微调阶段，总共不到 20,000 条轨迹数据。
Much of the game comes from two fine-tuning stages, on fewer than 20,000 trajectories in total.

133
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:31,856
数据的难度和可验证性可能比训练阶段的数量更重要。
The difficulty and verifiability of the data may matter more than the number of training stages.

134
00:10:32,046 --> 00:10:34,656
我的看法是，这些分数也需要谨慎对待。
My read is also that the scores deserve some caution.

135
00:10:34,766 --> 00:10:44,336
这些是多次运行中的最佳成绩，许多竞争对手的数据来自其他来源，
而且在受限的 HLE 和 Bio Mystery Bench 上，它仍然落后于最强的闭源模型。
They're the best of several runs, many rivals' numbers come from other sources, and
on restricted HLE and Bio Mystery Bench, it still trails the strongest closed models.

136
00:10:44,430 --> 00:10:47,616
真正的考验是其他人能否根据发布的配方复现出这些结果。
The real test is whether others can reproduce it from the released recipe.

137
00:10:47,776 --> 00:10:49,348
这就是今天的 Daily Frontier 论文。
That's today's Daily Frontier paper.

138
00:10:49,456 --> 00:10:50,976
论文链接就在描述栏里。
The paper is linked in the description.

